{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cognitive Load.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cognitive Load.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cognitive load cognitive load","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Cognitive Load.md","fileName":"Cognitive Load.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Cognitive Load","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Human Cognition]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human Cognition","Attention","Information Processing","3D Travel","Articulatory Distance","Semantic Distance","Interactivity Budget","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","advancedgamedesign.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cognitive Load.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cognitive Load.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cognitive load cognitive load","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Cognitive Load.md","fileName":"Cognitive Load.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Cognitive Load","heading":"Cognitive Load","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Cognitive load is the amount of mental work required by a task or situation. It is shaped by external task demands, such as difficulty and priority, and by internal limits in [[Attention]] and [[Information Processing]]. Skills and well-formed mental structures can reduce the effort needed.\n\nAn interface raises cognitive load when users must remember transient information, divide attention, interpret unclear mappings, or control a secondary task such as [[3D Travel]] while performing a primary task.\n\nEvaluation can combine subjective workload ratings with task-performance or physiological measures. Self-report is useful but is stronger when correlated with objective evidence.\n\nIn games, [[Articulatory Distance]] adds effort between intention and input, while [[Semantic Distance]] adds effort between feedback and understanding. These demands consume a finite [[Interactivity Budget]], so simultaneous fast action and complex reflection can overwhelm a player even when each demand is manageable alone.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human Cognition","Attention","Information Processing","3D Travel","Articulatory Distance","Semantic Distance","Interactivity Budget","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","advancedgamedesign.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cognitive Load.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cognitive Load.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cognitive load cognitive load","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Cognitive Load.md","fileName":"Cognitive Load.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Cognitive Load","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]\n[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human Cognition","Attention","Information Processing","3D Travel","Articulatory Distance","Semantic Distance","Interactivity Budget","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","advancedgamedesign.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}